{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q408652","formula":"C₈H₁₄ClN₅","hill":"C8H14ClN5","elements":["H","C","N","Cl"],"composition":{"C":8.0,"H":14.0,"N":5.0,"Cl":1.0},"names":{"en":"Atrazine","ru":"Атразин"},"descriptions":{"en":"Atrazine ( A-trə-zeen) is a chlorinated herbicide of the triazine class. It is used to prevent pre-emergence broadleaf weeds in crops such as maize (corn), soybean and sugarcane, and also in turf landscaping, such as golf courses and residential lawns. Atrazine is one of the most widely used herbicides in the United States, Canada, Australia, and Brazil, but has been banned in other countries including in the European Union and the Gulf Cooperation Council.","ru":"Атразин — тривиальное название гербицида из класса хлортриазинов. Используется для борьбы с широколиственными сорняками. Он был изобретён в 1958 году в лабораториях компании Geigy, вторым в серии 1,3,5-триазинов."},"fame":31,"pubchemCid":2256,"mass":215.68,"charge":0,"smiles":"CCNC1=NC(=NC(=N1)Cl)NC(C)C","inchikey":"MXWJVTOOROXGIU-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"6-chloro-4-N-ethyl-2-N-propan-2-yl-1,3,5-triazine-2,4-diamine","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"2256","atoms":28,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-1.442,"y":3.82,"z":-0.107,"el":"Cl"},{"x":2.16,"y":0.436,"z":0.106,"el":"N"},{"x":-2.287,"y":-1.053,"z":0.033,"el":"N"},{"x":-0.053,"y":-0.339,"z":0.07,"el":"N"},{"x":0.426,"y":2.011,"z":0.007,"el":"N"},{"x":-1.849,"y":1.249,"z":-0.031,"el":"N"},{"x":2.705,"y":-0.903,"z":0.166,"el":"C"},{"x":4.122,"y":-0.844,"z":0.72,"el":"C"},{"x":2.678,"y":-1.526,"z":-1.224,"el":"C"},{"x":0.805,"y":0.711,"z":0.06,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.903,"y":-2.429,"z":0.088,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.35,"y":0.004,"z":0.024,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.112,"y":-3.341,"z":0.124,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.902,"y":2.202,"z":-0.036,"el":"C"},{"x":